1
00:00:01,967 --> 00:00:05,033
It all started during our
first year of high school.

2
00:00:08,433 --> 00:00:10,300
(Class 1-2)

3
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:14,667
Wait, Serizawa, did you
break up with your girlfriend?

4
00:00:14,767 --> 00:00:16,800
Why? She seemed really nice.

5
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:18,333
Well...

6
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:19,500
Uh...

7
00:00:19,633 --> 00:00:22,600
Don't tell me it's the same old story?

8
00:00:23,133 --> 00:00:26,567
I've never really understood
what it feels like to "like" someone.

9
00:00:28,033 --> 00:00:28,733
Morning, Serizawa.

10
00:00:28,833 --> 00:00:29,933
Morning.

11
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:30,967
Morning, Serizawa.

12
00:00:31,067 --> 00:00:33,267
I enjoy talking to people.

13
00:00:33,367 --> 00:00:35,243
- And I'm happy when someone says they like me.
- What did you get on the test today?

14
00:00:35,267 --> 00:00:36,033
4:16.

15
00:00:36,133 --> 00:00:37,533
- What the heck?
- That's hilarious.

16
00:00:37,567 --> 00:00:38,000
We're taking off.

17
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:39,233
- Bye!
- See ya!

18
00:00:41,967 --> 00:00:43,333
But...

19
00:00:49,233 --> 00:00:52,333
I've never felt the urge
to get close to anyone.

20
00:00:54,967 --> 00:00:56,167
Not even once.

21
00:00:57,767 --> 00:01:00,700
(Please keep your voices down /
Library Committee: Serizawa, Takeuchi)

22
00:01:04,633 --> 00:01:06,767
So in the end,

23
00:01:06,867 --> 00:01:09,067
you just can't match their feelings,

24
00:01:09,167 --> 00:01:10,933
which makes them feel insecure.

25
00:01:11,033 --> 00:01:12,033
And before you know it,

26
00:01:12,067 --> 00:01:15,267
they end up calling it quits, right?

27
00:01:17,167 --> 00:01:20,533
I'm such a jerk.

28
00:01:21,833 --> 00:01:23,167
It can't be helped.

29
00:01:23,567 --> 00:01:26,800
You can't just logic your
way into liking someone.

30
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:30,000
I guess you're right.

31
00:01:30,567 --> 00:01:35,167
If you have time to chat, get to work.

32
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:38,200
All right.

33
00:02:07,433 --> 00:02:11,400
That day, I met him for the first time...

34
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:52,633
A guy whose name I didn't even know.

35
00:02:52,733 --> 00:02:55,767
He was just completely engrossed in a book.

36
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:59,200
That was literally it.

37
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:13,173
But for some reason, in that moment,

38
00:03:13,267 --> 00:03:14,833
I couldn't take my eyes off him.

39
00:03:24,733 --> 00:03:26,133
And my heart started racing.

40
00:03:27,333 --> 00:03:30,567
It was the first time in my
life I'd ever felt that way...

41
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,700
"Popular Serizawa Acts Weird Around Me"

42
00:04:15,633 --> 00:04:18,800
(Episode 7)

43
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:21,467
Oh, Serizawa, perfect timing.
The book returns over there...

44
00:04:21,567 --> 00:04:22,700
On it!

45
00:04:30,767 --> 00:04:35,267
From that day on, I couldn't
stop thinking about him.

46
00:04:37,567 --> 00:04:39,567
Rock, paper, scissors!

47
00:04:39,967 --> 00:04:41,767
Rock, paper, scissors!

48
00:04:41,867 --> 00:04:43,367
Look that way!

49
00:04:43,443 --> 00:04:44,256
[They're keeping a tally of wins]

50
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:45,000
Yes!

51
00:04:45,100 --> 00:04:47,000
Come on! How many times are you gonna win?

52
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:48,209
I'll take the win this time.

53
00:04:48,233 --> 00:04:49,700
Huh? Serizawa,

54
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:51,076
are you on library duty again today?

55
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:52,100
Yeah.

56
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:54,267
What's gotten into you lately?

57
00:04:54,367 --> 00:04:56,667
Just... nothing much.

58
00:04:57,133 --> 00:04:58,267
Huh?

59
00:05:20,833 --> 00:05:23,000
Suzuki, let's walk home together.

60
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:24,100
Okay.

61
00:05:24,567 --> 00:05:27,567
- You must be tired today too.
- Yeah.

62
00:05:27,667 --> 00:05:29,100
Exhausted.

63
00:05:31,233 --> 00:05:32,733
So his name is Suzuki.

64
00:05:35,467 --> 00:05:36,333
(Checkout Log)

65
00:05:36,433 --> 00:05:38,567
Suzuki...

66
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:43,133
Weird, it's not here.

67
00:05:44,033 --> 00:05:45,700
Has he never checked out a book?

68
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:50,633
He was so absorbed in it.

69
00:05:50,733 --> 00:05:52,367
What on earth was he reading?

70
00:06:07,633 --> 00:06:08,700
What are you looking up?

71
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:10,333
Oh, nothing. It's nothing.

72
00:06:10,433 --> 00:06:11,900
You've been really motivated lately.

73
00:06:47,267 --> 00:06:48,700
What on earth is he reading?

74
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:20,000
I just can't bring myself to say it.

75
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:21,600
It hurts so much.

76
00:07:21,700 --> 00:07:23,367
Just say it then.

77
00:07:23,933 --> 00:07:25,533
What on earth is he reading?

78
00:07:31,833 --> 00:07:34,367
If it were anyone else, I
could ask in a heartbeat.

79
00:07:34,467 --> 00:07:36,147
But when it comes to Suzuki, I just can't.

80
00:07:49,433 --> 00:07:51,033
What on earth is he reading?

81
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:07,467
What is he doing?

82
00:08:10,467 --> 00:08:11,867
Wanna join the judo club?

83
00:08:11,967 --> 00:08:13,067
Where did that come from?

84
00:08:13,167 --> 00:08:16,333
Come on, let's experience
our youth together!

85
00:08:16,433 --> 00:08:17,967
Maybe I should give it a try?

86
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:20,467
- Are you serious, Serizawa?
- For real?

87
00:08:20,567 --> 00:08:21,767
Just kidding!

88
00:08:22,133 --> 00:08:22,700
What about you?

89
00:08:22,800 --> 00:08:24,176
- I'm gonna throw you over my shoulder, you know?
- You...

90
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,067
That's totally not gonna work.

91
00:08:25,167 --> 00:08:26,167
It's not?

92
00:08:30,633 --> 00:08:31,700
Serizawa?

93
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:33,033
Seri...

94
00:08:33,267 --> 00:08:34,333
Hey, what's wrong?

95
00:08:34,433 --> 00:08:35,267
Hello?

96
00:08:35,367 --> 00:08:36,867
Serizawa!

97
00:08:38,867 --> 00:08:41,333
- Did that guy finally get motivated?
- Yeah, so sudden.

98
00:08:41,433 --> 00:08:42,433
He went that way.

99
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:05,640
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

100
00:09:05,733 --> 00:09:06,833
Please wait a moment.

101
00:09:20,673 --> 00:09:22,216
(Title: The Deep Sea and the Moon)
(Author: Ishibashi Tatakiware)

102
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:23,993
(The highly anticipated pure romance
BL novel gets a physical release!)

103
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:28,200
BL?

104
00:09:33,033 --> 00:09:35,900
Have you been secretly looking at me?

105
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:40,400
Actually, I have some feelings for you too.

106
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:42,000
I want to get to know you better.

107
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:44,867
I feel like if I get any closer,
there's no turning back.

108
00:09:44,967 --> 00:09:46,800
No turning back...

109
00:09:47,133 --> 00:09:50,500
Being stuck in this dilemma is killing me.

110
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,833
It hurts so much.

111
00:09:53,033 --> 00:09:54,400
Me too...

112
00:09:56,533 --> 00:09:58,500
Ah... what is this?

113
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:01,433
It's making my heart flutter so much.

114
00:10:03,867 --> 00:10:05,033
Wait.

115
00:10:05,367 --> 00:10:06,600
Hold on.

116
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:10,933
Is that why Suzuki made that expression?

117
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,733
Huh? Seriously?

118
00:10:21,367 --> 00:10:22,733
That's amazing.

119
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:26,467
So cute it's unfair...

120
00:10:29,333 --> 00:10:30,900
He's way too cute.

121
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:34,933
Once I say it, I won't be able to stop.

122
00:10:45,300 --> 00:10:46,500
So cute.

123
00:10:49,533 --> 00:10:51,467
Hey, are you okay?

124
00:10:51,867 --> 00:10:52,867
Yeah.

125
00:10:52,933 --> 00:10:53,933
I just dropped something.

126
00:10:53,967 --> 00:10:55,200
Let me help.

127
00:10:55,533 --> 00:10:56,833
Thanks.

128
00:10:57,433 --> 00:10:59,400
I want to know more about him.

129
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:06,500
I want to get closer to him.

130
00:11:12,833 --> 00:11:13,967
So cute.

131
00:11:14,733 --> 00:11:17,167
Suzuki, you've got something on your face.

132
00:11:20,533 --> 00:11:21,533
Thanks.

133
00:11:28,473 --> 00:11:29,513
Closer...

134
00:12:21,300 --> 00:12:22,633
Before I knew it,

135
00:12:22,733 --> 00:12:27,367
I was so obsessed with Suzuki
that even I felt stupid.

136
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:32,833
It's just that...

137
00:12:41,467 --> 00:12:45,067
I feel like if I say
anything, he'll run away.

138
00:12:47,867 --> 00:12:48,867
Suzuki.

139
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Morning.

140
00:12:50,433 --> 00:12:50,933
Morning.

141
00:12:51,033 --> 00:12:52,267
- Let's go.
- Yeah.

142
00:12:54,300 --> 00:12:55,933
Are you really sleepy?

143
00:12:56,033 --> 00:12:56,867
Did you do the homework?

144
00:12:56,967 --> 00:12:58,433
We had homework?

145
00:12:58,533 --> 00:12:59,533
Yeah.

146
00:12:59,833 --> 00:13:03,167
In the end, I never managed to talk to him.

147
00:13:03,267 --> 00:13:04,933
And the days just slipped by.

148
00:13:06,567 --> 00:13:09,047
Then, as our first year of high
school was coming to an end...

149
00:13:11,367 --> 00:13:12,167
What should we eat?

150
00:13:12,267 --> 00:13:12,967
Where's Suzuki?

151
00:13:13,067 --> 00:13:13,967
He's eating alone again?!

152
00:13:14,067 --> 00:13:18,033
That's ridiculous. He's
been acting so sneaky lately...

153
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:25,800
For some reason, Suzuki started
spending more and more time alone.

154
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:32,133
BL?

155
00:13:32,233 --> 00:13:33,667
Like, guys with guys?

156
00:13:33,767 --> 00:13:34,767
Is that what it means?

157
00:13:34,833 --> 00:13:35,667
No.

158
00:13:35,767 --> 00:13:37,033
That's gross.

159
00:13:40,667 --> 00:13:41,800
Seriously messed up.

160
00:13:41,900 --> 00:13:42,633
He definitely has it.

161
00:13:42,733 --> 00:13:44,167
No, I don't.

162
00:13:44,267 --> 00:13:47,067
Honestly, don't you think things have been
awkward with Suzuki lately?

163
00:13:47,167 --> 00:13:48,500
- I know, right!
- Yeah.

164
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:50,600
He's been reading BL all by himself lately.

165
00:13:50,700 --> 00:13:51,700
Plus,

166
00:13:51,733 --> 00:13:52,733
he's gotten super girly.

167
00:13:52,767 --> 00:13:54,433
- Oh, please no!
- Help me!

168
00:13:54,533 --> 00:13:56,267
Hey, you're taking it too far.

169
00:13:56,367 --> 00:13:57,500
- Huh?
- What?

170
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:59,967
You said it yourself
before, that BL is gross.

171
00:14:00,067 --> 00:14:00,833
Yeah.

172
00:14:00,933 --> 00:14:02,533
No, I just meant...

173
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:04,300
Hey, mind if I interrupt?

174
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:08,067
I thought I heard you
guys talking about BL.

175
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:10,667
Can I join in?

176
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:16,333
I'm interested in it too.

177
00:14:16,767 --> 00:14:17,767
BL.

178
00:14:19,133 --> 00:14:20,133
Uh...

179
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:23,000
Hey, let's go.

180
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,200
So lame.

181
00:15:24,833 --> 00:15:26,933
Hey, Suzuki.

182
00:15:29,433 --> 00:15:32,600
What did they say to you?

183
00:15:35,667 --> 00:15:37,267
Are you frustrated?

184
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:39,433
Does it hurt?

185
00:15:47,900 --> 00:15:51,500
Honestly, I was furious.

186
00:16:01,467 --> 00:16:04,000
I was mad at this world that hurt Suzuki.

187
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:10,933
And I was mad at myself for not
even being able to protect him.

188
00:16:20,467 --> 00:16:22,267
Serizawa, what are you doing?

189
00:16:22,367 --> 00:16:24,033
Weren't we supposed to grab food today?

190
00:16:24,133 --> 00:16:27,433
Oh, sorry. Um...
Can I ask you guys something?

191
00:16:27,533 --> 00:16:28,533
Yeah?

192
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:33,900
What would you do if I said I liked BL?

193
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,167
Huh? Where did that come from?

194
00:16:36,267 --> 00:16:39,167
Even if you liked BL, it wouldn't matter.

195
00:16:39,333 --> 00:16:40,333
Right?

196
00:16:40,900 --> 00:16:42,300
Yeah.

197
00:16:42,400 --> 00:16:44,900
Let's just go eat.

198
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:46,967
- Yeah.
- Exactly.

199
00:16:47,467 --> 00:16:49,567
There are people like that out there.

200
00:16:49,667 --> 00:16:51,967
So why should he be the one to get hurt?

201
00:16:55,967 --> 00:16:57,567
What happened?

202
00:16:58,100 --> 00:16:59,400
What's wrong?

203
00:16:59,500 --> 00:17:01,033
Want to talk about it?

204
00:17:01,133 --> 00:17:02,667
Want some chocolate?

205
00:17:03,067 --> 00:17:04,167
Here.

206
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,000
I've made up my mind.

207
00:17:07,367 --> 00:17:09,767
I'm going to be his friend.

208
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:11,433
Huh?

209
00:17:11,933 --> 00:17:15,433
I absolutely can't scare him,
nor can I overwhelm him.

210
00:17:15,533 --> 00:17:17,167
I'm going to approach him slowly.

211
00:17:17,267 --> 00:17:21,267
One day, I'll be someone he can
talk to about the things he loves.

212
00:17:21,367 --> 00:17:23,100
A best friend he can laugh with.

213
00:17:23,667 --> 00:17:25,107
What on earth are you talking about?

214
00:17:25,967 --> 00:17:30,500
All right! First, I need
to thoroughly study BL.

215
00:17:30,600 --> 00:17:32,267
Wait, what are you talking about?

216
00:17:33,967 --> 00:17:36,833
I'm going to be the King of BL!

217
00:17:40,967 --> 00:17:42,067
Huh?

218
00:17:43,867 --> 00:17:46,533
Then, I became a sophomore.

219
00:17:50,733 --> 00:17:53,533
Please let me be in
the same class as Suzuki.

220
00:17:55,367 --> 00:17:56,467
I'm heading out!

221
00:18:07,167 --> 00:18:09,300
I actually ended up in his class.

222
00:18:09,833 --> 00:18:11,267
(Class 2-1)
Huh? What?

223
00:18:11,367 --> 00:18:12,433
Tsundere!

224
00:18:12,533 --> 00:18:14,267
I'm not a tsundere.

225
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:23,733
Thank goodness.

226
00:18:25,533 --> 00:18:29,600
I thank the BL gods from
the bottom of my heart.

227
00:18:30,353 --> 00:18:32,919
(10: Hajime Suzuki
11: Haruto Serizawa)

228
00:18:55,933 --> 00:18:58,000
Suzuki, you dropped this.

229
00:18:58,600 --> 00:18:59,800
Here.

230
00:19:00,933 --> 00:19:03,867
Th-Thanks.

231
00:19:07,833 --> 00:19:09,367
That being said...

232
00:19:11,133 --> 00:19:13,067
Are we going bowling or to karaoke today?

233
00:19:13,167 --> 00:19:15,467
Nah, let's hit the gym today.

234
00:19:15,567 --> 00:19:16,867
- No way.
- Back off.

235
00:19:16,967 --> 00:19:17,967
- No.
- You can't.

236
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:19,000
Serizawa.

237
00:19:19,100 --> 00:19:21,633
- Ah! I heard the party room is open.
- Seriously?

238
00:19:21,733 --> 00:19:23,009
- Can it fit a lot of people?
- Yeah...

239
00:19:23,033 --> 00:19:24,233
Is there space over there?

240
00:19:24,333 --> 00:19:26,367
- Really?
- Yeah, it's open.

241
00:19:26,467 --> 00:19:28,400
- Let's go if it's open.
- That sounds good.

242
00:19:28,667 --> 00:19:29,800
We're pretty lucky.

243
00:19:29,900 --> 00:19:31,000
Suzuki.

244
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:33,667
We're all going to hang out.

245
00:19:33,767 --> 00:19:35,567
Do you want to come along?

246
00:19:37,667 --> 00:19:41,067
Sorry, I'm not great with
these kinds of gatherings.

247
00:19:43,233 --> 00:19:44,000
I see.

248
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:45,380
Sorry for springing this on you.

249
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:47,920
Let's hang out next time we get the chance.

250
00:19:56,733 --> 00:20:01,033
But closing the distance between Suzuki
and me wasn't going to be that easy.

251
00:20:01,433 --> 00:20:03,033
(Plot Outline Notebook)

252
00:20:08,133 --> 00:20:09,767
It's a story outline.

253
00:20:11,567 --> 00:20:14,200
That day, a miracle happened.

254
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:22,433
(Serizawa Haruto, Sakuragaoka High School,
2nd Year) (Popular guy, extroverted, athletic)

255
00:20:33,433 --> 00:20:36,100
This "Serizawa Haruto"
written in this notebook...

256
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:37,433
It's about me, right?

257
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:38,667
Since then...

258
00:20:38,767 --> 00:20:39,767
Please.

259
00:20:39,833 --> 00:20:41,100
Give it to me.

260
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:42,767
Let me be your first reader.

261
00:20:42,867 --> 00:20:44,833
After learning Suzuki's secret,

262
00:20:44,933 --> 00:20:47,333
I became his first reader.

263
00:20:48,867 --> 00:20:50,267
We became friends.

264
00:20:51,867 --> 00:20:53,300
We went on dates.

265
00:20:55,567 --> 00:20:56,833
Suzuki.

266
00:20:57,500 --> 00:20:58,800
Look at me.

267
00:21:01,300 --> 00:21:02,833
We kissed.

268
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:07,133
And now, here we are.

269
00:21:08,367 --> 00:21:09,367
I'm sorry.

270
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:13,233
I really can't go on a date with you.

271
00:21:16,167 --> 00:21:19,000
Why not?

272
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:24,533
I...

273
00:21:24,633 --> 00:21:28,600
I finally understand

274
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:31,967
what these feelings are.

275
00:21:32,067 --> 00:21:34,633
I have someone I like.

276
00:21:39,467 --> 00:21:41,867
"Library Rules No food or
drinks allowed. Please keep quiet."

277
00:21:44,833 --> 00:21:46,033
Suzuki.

278
00:21:47,700 --> 00:21:48,967
Serizawa.

279
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:53,267
Now, whenever I call his name,

280
00:21:53,367 --> 00:21:55,467
he always turns around with a smile.

281
00:21:57,767 --> 00:21:59,100
But...

282
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:02,200
That isn't enough.

283
00:22:06,500 --> 00:22:07,967
What are you reading?

284
00:22:10,267 --> 00:22:12,933
It's a manga I bought yesterday.

285
00:22:13,033 --> 00:22:14,267
Look at this.

286
00:22:14,467 --> 00:22:16,167
Isn't this uke way too dense?

287
00:22:16,567 --> 00:22:18,267
Huh? Where?

288
00:22:18,867 --> 00:22:20,100
Look here.

289
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:23,176
The seme is pursuing him so relentlessly, and
his feelings are written all over his face.

290
00:22:23,200 --> 00:22:24,700
Yet he hasn't noticed at all.

291
00:22:25,133 --> 00:22:26,400
You're right.

292
00:22:26,867 --> 00:22:28,233
So cute.

293
00:22:35,167 --> 00:22:36,867
I really hope he figures it out soon.

294
00:22:38,733 --> 00:22:42,733
He's the first person
I've ever loved in my life.

295
00:22:44,833 --> 00:22:46,400
We should probably head back.

296
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:47,933
No.

297
00:22:48,600 --> 00:22:50,133
- Serizawa?
- No.

298
00:22:50,333 --> 00:22:51,333
I don't want to.

299
00:22:51,667 --> 00:22:52,833
No...

300
00:22:52,933 --> 00:22:54,733
But we have to go back.

301
00:22:54,833 --> 00:22:57,700
Of course I won't let him get away.

302
00:22:58,333 --> 00:22:59,567
No.

303
00:22:59,900 --> 00:23:02,376
(Next Episode Preview) Suzuki, let's
make some summer memories together.

304
00:23:02,400 --> 00:23:03,400
I have someone I like.

305
00:23:03,433 --> 00:23:06,933
He's cute, gentle, and works really hard.

306
00:23:07,033 --> 00:23:09,067
Do you know who I'm talking about?

307
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:11,033
- Hey...
- That's awesome.

308
00:23:11,200 --> 00:23:14,633
(This drama is purely fictional.)
There's one person who fits all of that.
